ween 12.0 days and 15.0 days, and the same Pilot Line manages EV_battery, ceramic_substrate, and steel_rod there. Finished CPUs and EV_batteries are then sent from the Pilot Line to the Storage Facility with immediate transfer. Starting stock is very large on the finished side, with 4822498 units of CPU and 804033 units of EV_battery on hand initially. EV_battery inventory also has a shortage cost of $10.914 per unit and is checked every 1 day. On the demand side, Schneider Electric buys CPU with order arrivals following an exponential pattern averaging 55.0 days. Order size is normally centered around 4677112.0 units, varying by about 1341987.0 units. CPU shipments to Schneider Electric take exactly 20.0 days, unmet demand is backordered, the selling price is $2075.074 per unit, and customers pay 70.0 days after delivery. Infineon Technologies purchases EV_battery with orders coming anywhere from 26.0 days to 55.0 days apart, and each order is fixed at 4466540.0 units. Delivery to Infineon Technologies takes 29.0 days, available stock is shipped and the remainder is lost, the sales price is $3853.182 per unit, and customer payment arrives between 13.0 days and 45.0 days. The model runs for 365 days total, with the first 30 days treated as warm-up, and 5 replications are used.

